From 2667db8518bbf1a30f67985d96570fc0c63b2b2f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:20:32 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 148/159] tls: the fingerprint fallback tries the ClientHello
 without X25519MLKEM768 first, then firefox

Measured in October 2026: the Russian DPI freezes the connections of chrome (Chrome 133
with the X25519MLKEM768 key share), safari and randomized when many are made to one
server at once, REALITY and plain TLS alike; the same ClientHello without the key share
and firefox pass. With the fallback on, a client tries the configured fingerprint
without the key share, then firefox (which REALITY servers since Xray-core v26.9.8 take,
unlike the former), then the fingerprint as it is. A refusal by the server moves it on at
once; an unanswered ClientHello as before. One dial probes while the others wait; the
choice is kept in the cache file and checked again after a day. The list of
fingerprints of the option is no longer used.
